dist/
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tar.zst

# Byte-code left behind by running the tools locally. Committing it once was enough: a stale .pyc
# beside a newer .py is a file that can be imported instead of the source.
__pycache__/

# The private half of the signing key. It belongs in this repository's Actions secrets, which is
# what signs, and in a backup outside every working tree — never here, whatever the examples in
# docs/ used to say. An index signed by a key that leaked is an index that can be forged, and the
# public key is compiled into MixEngine, so recovering from either a leak or a loss needs an
# application release. `*.key` below is the belt for this brace.
minisign.key
*.key

# Implementation plans — local working notes for one stretch of work, never shared or referenced.
# The design document that outlives the branch is its spec, under docs/superpowers/specs/.
docs/superpowers/plans/
